# Animated Indicator List — sectioned actor/film list with a horizontal header
# row on top; scrolling slides the header row and stretches a black underline
# to the current section (measured on the UI thread, interpolated per frame);
# touching a header scrolls the list to that section.
# What this test covers: header taps walking every section to the last one
# (scrollToIndex + header row translation), slow manual scrolls back up through
# section boundaries (indicator width/offset interpolation), a fast fling down
# to the end of the list (clamped extrapolation), and rapid header taps that
# interrupt an in-flight scrollToIndex.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/animated-indicator-list"
wait 2000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 30000
wait "text" "AL PACINO" 30000
wait "text" "The Irishman" 8000
wait 1000
# Tap AL PACINO: list jumps, header row slides left.
press 234 90
wait 1200
wait "text" "LEONARDO DICAPRIO" 8000
# Next header each time (second slot in the row).
press 185 90
wait 1200
wait "text" "Home Alone" 8000
press 185 90
wait 1200
wait "text" "BRAD PITT" 8000
press 270 90
wait 1200
wait "text" "Fight Club" 8000
# Slow manual scrolls back up across section boundaries (never past the top:
# a pull-down at the top is the app's close gesture).
gesture pan 200 300 0 300 900
wait 600
gesture pan 200 300 0 300 900
wait 600
gesture pan 200 300 0 250 900
wait 800
# Fling down to the end of the list.
swipe 200 750 200 200
swipe 200 750 200 200
swipe 200 750 200 200
wait 1500
wait "text" "Benjamin Button" 8000
# Back up a bit, then rapid header taps interrupting scrollToIndex.
gesture pan 200 300 0 400 900
wait 800
press 185 90
wait 120
press 270 90
wait 120
press 185 90
wait 120
press 250 90
wait 1500
gesture pan 200 700 0 -300 600
wait 1000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 15000
press "role=\"button\" label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
